    "senderName": "NWS Hanford CA",
    "headline": "Red Flag Warning issued October 16 at 5:34PM PDT until October 16 at 10:00PM PDT by NWS Hanford CA",
    "description": "...RED FLAG WARNING REMAINS IN EFFECT UNTIL 10 PM PDT THIS\nEVENING DUE TO WIND AND LOW RELATIVE HUMIDITY FOR CENTRAL SIERRA,\nNORTH KINGS RIVER, SEQUOIA KINGS, LAKE ISABELLA, TEHACHAPI AREA,\nAND FORT TEJON...\n\n* AFFECTED AREA...Fire weather zone 592 Central Sierra. Fire\nweather zone 593 North Kings River. Fire weather zone 594\nSequoia Kings. Fire weather zone 595 Lake Isabella. Elevations\nfrom 4,000 feet and above.\n\n* TIMING...Until 10 PM PDT this evening.\n\n* WINDS...East winds 10 to 20 mph with gusts up to 40 mph.\n\n* RELATIVE HUMIDITY...Minimum relative humidity between 15 to 25\npercent.\n\n* IMPACTS...Any fires that develop will likely spread rapidly.\nOutdoor burning is not recommended.",
    "instruction": "Please advise the appropriate officials or fire crews in the\nfield of this Red Flag Warning.\n\nA Red Flag Warning is issued when we identify weather conditions\nthat promote rapid spread of fire which may become life-\nthreatening. This does not mean there is a fire. These conditions\nare either occurring now or will begin soon. It is important to\nhave multiple ways to receive information from authorities.",
